      "title": "[Samādhirājasūtra]",
      "description": "Section: R [Samādhirājasūtra] Written in the southern Turkestan Brāhmī (main type). Three times the Central Asian vowel -e is written with a long stroke and a flag-shaped hook to the right, but only once apparently because the Indian -e otherwise would have touched the preceding anusvāra. Five times the looped diacritic sign for -i is written. Cf. the description in AKh I, p. 297: “D. VI.1. MS. on paper; Brāhmī; No. 28. Note xv. Lefthand fragment, 4 1/2\" 3\", with string-hole, of a leaf numbered 70. Full size, probably 18\" 3\". Language: Sanskrit. Characters: upright Gupta of seventh or eighth century. Contents: apparently some Buddhist canonic",
