      "title": "[Saddharmapuṇḍarīkasūtra]",
      "description": "Section: R [Saddharmapuṇḍarīkasūtra] Written in the southern Turkestan Brāhmī (main type). Six times the Central Asian vowel -e is written, but only once apparently because the Indian -e otherwise would have touched the preceding superscribed vowel. There are two separated fragments of Kha. i.60. Fragment Or.8212/25(3) is given here in italics and Kha. i.209 in bold. Parallels: Ka 93b2-95a3; Otani (Lushun) SLLMC A-5 v4-8; SHT 4303, fragm. 17r5-v5 [ed. Wille 2000]; SI P/11.1 fragm. 3r2-4 [ed. BB 33, pp. 129f., No. 46]; KN 87.8(?)- 90.2; Wa 38.6(ḥ)-39.33, 214.25(?)-216.20. transliteration: l.1: 1 /// + + [m]. .. .. .. [s]. .. + + /// nasya nirg",
